#7501
"A Glowing Cave"
"You are in a large, rounded cave acting as a junction of multiple tunnels. 
The walls of the cave are coated in a glowing lichen that provides a gentle
greenish-yellow glow throughout the area.  The dull light is just enough to
let you see by.  Several twining tendrils of shuvana roots form a natural set
of stairs leading from the ground clear up to a hole in the ceiling.  A gentle
breeze comes from the hole above you indicating that it is a way out of the
caves and into the forest overhead.  To the north, west and south wide tunnels
lead away but to the east rests an ornate archway set into the stone of the
cave wall.
"
