#7504
"A Small, Glowing Cavern"
"The walls of this cavern are far enough apart that a horse could easily canter
about a short ways, provided you could even fit a horse through the caves to
get here.  Unlike the majority of the other caves and tunnels on this level,
there is very little of the glowing lichen here with only a sparse smattering
on the vaulted cavern ceiling high over head.  There is barely enough lichen
to provide any light and it looks like there is no lichen at all on the floor
around a dark opening leading further down.  Jagged cracks in the wall lead
away to the south and east where considerably brighter glows indicate more
profusion of the lichen.
"
