#7518
"A Glowing Cul-de-sac"
"You are inside a small dead-end tunnel that flares out then back in
forming a natural cul-de-sac.  A column of stone rests in the middle of the
room where a stalactite and stalagmite finally met after millenia of forming. 
Smaller stalactites and stalagmites dot the area around the column and a pool
of water has formed at their base from the dripping water that has created the
rock formations.  Glowing lichen grows on the walls and roof in profusion,
lighting the room and throwing reflections of the light that dance about every
time water drips into the pool.
"
