#7561
"A Glowing Cul-de-sac"
"The tunnel coming in from the north terminates rather suddenly at an
unexpected sight here in this cul-de-sac.  Porous rock along the top of the
southern wall has allowed water to slowly seep through over a long period of
time and the southern wall has slowly changed to accommodate the water running
over it as well as the sediment carried with it.  The southern wall is now
covered in irregular clusters and rough knobs of crystalline formations that
sparkle in the greenish-yellow glow of the glowing lichen on the walls as
water continues to slowly seep over the wall.
"
