#7624
"A Hidden Laboratory"
"Thick, beams of wood reinforce the natural stone of this cave and it is
apparent someone went to an effort to smooth the walls to a uniform finish.
Several simple, low tables and benches are pressed up against the walls and
are covered in a debris of cracked, useless containers and burned out candle
stubs.  In the center of the room a firepit filled with glowing coals covered
by a thick iron grill.  Overhead a neatly drilled hole allows the smoke to
waft away up some shaft and out of the cave.  The glow from the wide firepit
alone is enough to bathe the room in a dull, red light that would cast
everything a vision of blood and shadows if it were the only light used.
"
""
